#import "../ch4/src.typ": *

The F-35A is controllable up to its limit of 50° angle of attack: in flight tests it was flown to the limit within four flights#aoa50. At the limit the pedals still turn the nose quickly#hanche. There is no public description of a stall, a departure or a spin of the jet, nor of a recovery (@emergency-control): open.

The low-speed warning tone is the limit for manoeuvring#afi[paragraph 3.13.2].

#in-sim[
  - With the stick fully back the jet holds about 50° and stays under control: it keeps its roll and its pedals nearly to the limit. The speed falls fast.
  - A full push brings the angle of attack below 15° within about 6 seconds.
  - There is no departure, no deep stall and no spin. In level flight at 1 g the least speed is about 128 kt at sea level with full fuel.
  - The aerodynamics above 30° are inferred: no F-35 data is public.
  - #term("Not modelled"): the buffet at high angle of attack, any departure.
]
